=== REASONING ===
1. DriveHandler already has db *database.DB → create signalLogReader in constructor (no router change).
2. VehicleHandler lacks db → add SetSignalLogReader setter (like SetTelemetryHandler), one-line router wiring.
3. driveTelemetryMappings: field names match old DriveTelemetryReading JSON tags (speed, battery_level,
   inside_temp, etc.) so camelCaseKeys preserves frontend contract.
4. positionMappings: field names match old Position model JSON tags (speed_mph, elevation_m, heading, etc.)
5. Telemetry timestamp: PivotFlat returns "ts" → rename to "created_at" to match old model.
6. Position timestamp: PivotFlat "ts" matches Position model's "ts" — no rename needed.
7. Drive Get handler: replaced embedded *models.Drive struct with explicit map to include both
   telemetry and positions from signal_log. Errors on telemetry/positions are warnings (graceful fallback).
8. In-progress drives (no end_ts): use time.Now() as end timestamp, same pattern as before.

